# Store every text file with LF endings, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, so without this the committed
# blobs are LF but the working tree is CRLF. Biome's formatter expects LF, which
# meant `pnpm lint` reported ~330 byte-identical, otherwise-clean files as
# formatting errors on Windows and could never pass locally.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what counts as text, so binaries are left alone and
# need no explicit entries here.
* text=auto eol=lf
